{"command": "echo "The question asks specifically about OCS as defined in 43 U.S. Code § 1331, which defines the Outer Continental Shelf lands. In the Treasury Bulletin, this refers to "rents and royalties on the Outer Continental Shelf lands" which is listed as an undistributed offsetting receipt.

Based on the Treasury Bulletin data for calendar year 2016, the lowest amount (smallest absolute value) of recorded OCS rents and royalties was 56 million dollars in January 2016.

Final Answer: 56""}
